Sol Atlas
---------
Parts of the EVA route & scouting feature (src/lib/eva-route/) are derived from Sol Atlas by
The SOL Explorers, https://github.com/saracen66/the-sol-explorers
(commit 9e1b2e0dc9ea8835b1edde0d1af73e551a72b231), licensed under the Apache License,
Version 2.0. A copy of that licence, copied unchanged from the upstream repository, is in
LICENSES/Apache-2.0-Sol-Atlas.txt. The upstream repository has no NOTICE file and its source
files carry no copyright headers; its README states the Apache-2.0 licence.

Files derived from Sol Atlas (each file's header states the changes):
  src/lib/eva-route/sol-atlas-eva.ts   from src/terrain/eva.js (EVA O2 / time model, Pandolf
                                       metabolic rate). Modified 2026-11-14: TypeScript port;
                                       the unpressurised-rover option, the per-sample timeline,
                                       the radiation-dose helper and the daylight checks removed.
                                       Equations, constants and defaults unchanged.
  src/lib/eva-route/pathfind.ts        from src/terrain/pathfinding.js (8-neighbour A*), by way of
                                       the MarsScout prototype. Modified 2026-11-14: hard no-go
                                       cells and slope limit, caller-supplied passability, no
                                       diagonal corner cutting, cell-index API, TypeScript port.

No Sol Atlas data files, images, sound, user interface, deployment configuration or branding
are included. MDI uses its own verified CTX terrain crop and traverse data (src/data/).

MarsScout prototype
-------------------
The other src/lib/eva-route/ modules (grid, knowledge, traversal, truth, planner, budget,
assumptions, scouting, options, mission, world) are adapted from the MarsScout prototype
written for this project on 2026-11-14 (a separate, unpublished working copy that itself
derives from Sol Atlas as listed above). docs/EVA_ROUTE_SCOUTING.md lists every file and change.

Data
----
Real data used by the feature (sources as recorded in src/data/sources.json):
  - MRO CTX Jezero DEM (20 m) and CTX Jezero mosaic (controlled), NASA Solar System Treks
    (Mars Trek), JPL: ids trek-jezero-ctx-dtm and trek-jezero-ctx-ortho; bounded crop built by
    scripts/build-ctx-terrain.mjs (docs/TERRAIN_3D.md).
  - Perseverance (Mars 2020) Path, NASA Solar System Treks (Mars Trek), JPL: id
    trek-perseverance-traverse (historical positions; docs/GEO_DATA.md).
  - Sample site positions: Mars 2020 Initial Reports Volume 4 (Sample Dossier), NASA Planetary
    Data System, Geosciences Node: id pds-m2020-initial-reports-vol4.
Everything else in the EVA route view is SIMULATED: the habitat, the surveyed areas, the scout
rover and its model, the hidden ground hazards, the crew surface rules and the decision weights
(src/data/prototype/eva-scouting.json, src/lib/eva-route/).

